WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.670
In the creeds, Christians
call God Almighty.

2
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.190
All-powerful.

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.220
Christians also call God
benevolent: all-loving.

4
00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:12.430
And Christians believe
every wrong matters to God,

5
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.610
because God judges fairly.

6
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.120
Power, love and judgement.

7
00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:20.880
Side by side, they can seem to
pull in different directions.

8
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:25.720
So how can one God be all-powerful,
all-loving and a fair judge,

9
00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:27.010
all at once?

10
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.160
In this mission, you'll build a web
of the words Christians use for God,

11
00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.610
from omnipotent to benevolent.

12
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.060
Then you'll match each
word to its meaning,

13
00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:38.200
and spot the common mix-ups.

14
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:43.220
Your mission: find out how Christians
believe one God can be all-powerful,

15
00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.480
all-loving and a fair judge.
